**Date:** 29 October 2026 · **Deciders:** support desk

## Context

[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged 412 reports under one subject and one status: known, one fix
queued. Subject-matching dedupe ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) is fast,
but it does not read the report. `src/lib/kb/causes.ts` already computes a real cause per report,
and `CauseTable` already flags a second cause inside #4471 as "not this ticket — no ticket of its
own." `desk-notes.json` already footnotes five reports as something else again. Nobody opened
tickets for either.

<Callout kind="warn">
One subject line, three bugs. #4471 as filed covers only the first.
</Callout>

## What #4471 actually holds

| cause | reports | what breaks | tickets |
|---|---|---|---|
| parser | 379 | the shared parser reads every date month-first; a day-first tenant on `booking-v2` or any non-form channel gets the day and month swapped. Counted the way `groupByCause()` counts it: includes the 5 `oneDayMove` reports below, which the cause-matcher still sorts in here. | ticket A |
| hint | 33 | on `booking-v3`, the form's own hint tells a day-first tenant's people to type month-first; the form then reads what they typed the tenant's (day-first) way. Same symptom, different code path. | ticket B |
| one-day move | 5 | the date is right, only off by a single day; no month/day swap is involved. Flagged in `desk-notes.json` as `oneDayMove`, filed under `parser` above by the cause-matcher, worth its own ticket because the symptom does not match either bug. | ticket C |

379 + 33 = 412, counted the way the kb itself counts a cause group. The 5 `oneDayMove` reports are
a subset of the 379, not a fourth bucket: still worth their own ticket, because the desk's
cause-matcher placed them by channel and form, never by what the report says.

## Decision

Open one ticket per cause above, each carrying its own count, instead of leaving all three under
#4471's single "known" status. #4471 stays as the record of the merge; the three new tickets carry
the fixes.

## Consequences

- Engineering can ship the `hint` fix (read the form the way its own hint says) without it hiding
  behind the `parser` fix (locale-aware parsing).
- The five `oneDayMove` reports stop being miscounted as evidence for the month/day swap; they get
  looked at as their own, much smaller, problem.
- `#4471`'s "known. one issue, one fix queued" is no longer accurate and should be corrected to
  point at the three tickets.

